1
00:00:01,000 --> 00:00:03,000
[Leorio] Yeah. It looks real.

2
00:00:03,000 --> 00:00:05,000
And there’s a video attached to it.

3
00:00:05,000 --> 00:00:06,000
We’ve got two targets.

4
00:00:07,000 --> 00:00:08,000
A man and a woman.

5
00:00:09,000 --> 00:00:10,000
I’ll head out right now,

6
00:00:10,000 --> 00:00:12,000
so you just meet me there.

7
00:00:12,000 --> 00:00:13,000
[Gon] Got it.

8
00:00:13,000 --> 00:00:15,000
-Come on. Let’s go!
-Okay.

9
00:00:22,000 --> 00:00:25,000
[theme song playing]

10
00:01:36,000 --> 00:01:41,000
PURSUIT X AND X ANALYSIS

11
00:01:43,000 --> 00:01:46,000
[narrator] Following a tip
about the Phantom Troupe,

12
00:01:46,000 --> 00:01:48,000
Gon and his friends move out.

13
00:01:49,000 --> 00:01:52,000
Once there, they encounter
Machi and Nobunaga.

14
00:01:53,000 --> 00:01:56,000
But the pair is not simply waiting around
to be caught.

15
00:01:57,000 --> 00:02:00,000
What do you think?
Did Uvo really get himself killed?

16
00:02:01,000 --> 00:02:03,000
Probably, yeah.

17
00:02:05,000 --> 00:02:07,000
Uvo may have been a brute,
but he wasn’t stupid.

18
00:02:08,000 --> 00:02:10,000
I certainly can’t disagree with you there.

19
00:02:11,000 --> 00:02:13,000
[Nobunaga] It didn’t matter
how tough his opponent was,

20
00:02:14,000 --> 00:02:16,000
he always had the wits and experience
to prevail.

21
00:02:16,000 --> 00:02:18,000
[phone ringing]

22
00:02:19,000 --> 00:02:20,000
[woman] Yeah, hello?

23
00:02:20,000 --> 00:02:22,000
[Leorio] I’m the guy who posted the ad.

24
00:02:23,000 --> 00:02:25,000
[woman] Well, you’re late! Where are you?

25
00:02:25,000 --> 00:02:26,000
Please stop looking around.

26
00:02:27,000 --> 00:02:28,000
We can see you, so don’t worry.

27
00:02:29,000 --> 00:02:32,000
Is that them?
The couple right behind your boyfriend?

28
00:02:32,000 --> 00:02:35,000
I’m wiring the money to your account.
Confirm receipt.

29
00:02:38,000 --> 00:02:39,000
Really?

30
00:02:41,000 --> 00:02:42,000
[woman] Let’s go! Come on!

31
00:02:44,000 --> 00:02:47,000
[Machi] But Uvo didn’t come back
this time.

32
00:02:47,000 --> 00:02:50,000
Has he ever been this late
without letting us know before?

33
00:02:51,000 --> 00:02:53,000
You heard what he said, didn’t you?

34
00:02:54,000 --> 00:02:55,000
He wasn’t coming back

35
00:02:55,000 --> 00:02:57,000
‘til he settled the score
with the chain user.

36
00:02:58,000 --> 00:03:01,000
Yeah, I heard. That’s why I said probably.

37
00:03:01,000 --> 00:03:03,000
I didn’t say that I was sure he was dead.

38
00:03:04,000 --> 00:03:05,000
[Nobunaga] That your hunch?

39
00:03:06,000 --> 00:03:07,000
[Machi] Just a hunch.

40
00:03:08,000 --> 00:03:11,000
[Nobunaga] Well… your hunches are right,
more often than not.

41
00:03:11,000 --> 00:03:14,000
[Leorio] Okay.
We should decide our next move.

42
00:03:14,000 --> 00:03:17,000
So how should we go about
capturing these two?

43
00:03:17,000 --> 00:03:19,000
[Killua] We don’t.

44
00:03:20,000 --> 00:03:22,000
Look, they’re way out of our league.
It’s not happening.

45
00:03:23,000 --> 00:03:25,000
[yells] Oh, come on!
We won’t know until we try,

46
00:03:25,000 --> 00:03:28,000
and besides,
why didn’t you mention this before?!

47
00:03:28,000 --> 00:03:30,000
Stop yelling. They’ll notice us.

48
00:03:31,000 --> 00:03:32,000
But it’s the truth.

49
00:03:32,000 --> 00:03:34,000
I knew it as soon as I saw them.

50
00:03:36,000 --> 00:03:39,000
A while back my dad killed a Spider
for a job.

51
00:03:40,000 --> 00:03:41,000
-[Gon] Huh?
-What?

52
00:03:42,000 --> 00:03:43,000
He doesn’t complain much…

53
00:03:44,000 --> 00:03:47,000
but he said the job
wasn’t worth the price.

54
00:03:48,000 --> 00:03:51,000
And that is the highest compliment
he gives a target.

55
00:03:52,000 --> 00:03:54,000
He even got all of us together

56
00:03:55,000 --> 00:03:57,000
and told us we should steer clear
of the Phantom Troupe.

57
00:03:59,000 --> 00:04:01,000
But that was years ago,

58
00:04:01,000 --> 00:04:03,000
so I thought we might stand a chance.

59
00:04:04,000 --> 00:04:06,000
[Leorio] They can’t be that strong…

60
00:04:06,000 --> 00:04:07,000
can they?

61
00:04:07,000 --> 00:04:10,000
Just imagine if the people
sitting at that table

62
00:04:10,000 --> 00:04:11,000
were both Hisokas.

63
00:04:14,000 --> 00:04:15,000
I guess...

64
00:04:15,000 --> 00:04:18,000
it’s safe to say that
that’s a lot more than we can handle.

65
00:04:18,000 --> 00:04:21,000
Okay. So, what do you think
they’re doing here?

66
00:04:21,000 --> 00:04:22,000
They’re dating.

67
00:04:22,000 --> 00:04:24,000
It’s a date. Right?

68
00:04:24,000 --> 00:04:25,000
Wait… Is it really?

69
00:04:25,000 --> 00:04:26,000
[Killua] No, of course not.

70
00:04:27,000 --> 00:04:29,000
They noticed that other couple
behind them.

71
00:04:30,000 --> 00:04:33,000
I can tell they’re paying close attention
to their surroundings.

72
00:04:34,000 --> 00:04:36,000
I thought they were just being cautious

73
00:04:36,000 --> 00:04:37,000
since the Mafia’s after them.

74
00:04:39,000 --> 00:04:40,000
But if that was the case,

75
00:04:40,000 --> 00:04:43,000
they wouldn’t be sitting in a public area
like that.

76
00:04:44,000 --> 00:04:47,000
Instead, they act like
they don’t have a care in the world.

77
00:04:49,000 --> 00:04:51,000
They’re waiting
for someone to find them,

78
00:04:51,000 --> 00:04:52,000
acting as bait

79
00:04:52,000 --> 00:04:54,000
and trying to draw out their prey.

80
00:04:56,000 --> 00:04:57,000
We’re being observed.

81
00:04:58,000 --> 00:05:00,000
And they’re not amateurs.

82
00:05:01,000 --> 00:05:03,000
[Nobunaga] Yeah.
I can’t tell where they are,

83
00:05:03,000 --> 00:05:05,000
they’re watching us.

84
00:05:05,000 --> 00:05:06,000
[Machi] Is it the chain user?

85
00:05:07,000 --> 00:05:08,000
[Nobunaga] No idea.

86
00:05:08,000 --> 00:05:09,000
But if it is,

87
00:05:09,000 --> 00:05:12,000
the Boss gave us free reign
to do whatever we want.

88
00:05:13,000 --> 00:05:14,000
I don’t know about you,

89
00:05:15,000 --> 00:05:17,000
but I got the distinct impression
he wants us to recruit him.

90
00:05:18,000 --> 00:05:19,000
Machi...

91
00:05:20,000 --> 00:05:22,000
The Boss said to find him
and bring him back.

92
00:05:22,000 --> 00:05:24,000
Those were our only orders.

93
00:05:25,000 --> 00:05:29,000
Come on, you haven’t forgotten all
about the unspoken rule, have you?

94
00:05:29,000 --> 00:05:33,000
“Alive or dead
and by any means necessary”?

95
00:05:34,000 --> 00:05:36,000
You’re welcome
to interpret the Boss’s orders

96
00:05:36,000 --> 00:05:37,000
any way you see fit,

97
00:05:38,000 --> 00:05:41,000
but you can’t force me
into agreeing with you.

98
00:05:41,000 --> 00:05:43,000
Don’t put words in my mouth, all right?

99
00:05:43,000 --> 00:05:46,000
Besides, you’re the one forcing the issue.

100
00:05:52,000 --> 00:05:54,000
The atmosphere has changed.

101
00:05:54,000 --> 00:05:56,000
I’m getting a bad feeling…

102
00:05:56,000 --> 00:05:57,000
Do you think they noticed us?

103
00:05:58,000 --> 00:05:59,000
Not yet.

104
00:05:59,000 --> 00:06:00,000
We’re still in the clear.

105
00:06:00,000 --> 00:06:01,000
You sure about that?

106
00:06:02,000 --> 00:06:04,000
Remember, I can’t use Zetsu
to mask my presence

107
00:06:04,000 --> 00:06:06,000
like the two of you.

108
00:06:06,000 --> 00:06:08,000
Zetsu would attract attention,

109
00:06:08,000 --> 00:06:10,000
so we can’t use it here.

110
00:06:10,000 --> 00:06:13,000
They can sense Nen,
but they aren’t trying.

111
00:06:14,000 --> 00:06:16,000
They’re looking at people in the area

112
00:06:16,000 --> 00:06:19,000
trying to find anyone who acts suspicious.

113
00:06:19,000 --> 00:06:20,000
Be careful.

114
00:06:20,000 --> 00:06:22,000
And wipe those looks off your faces.

115
00:06:23,000 --> 00:06:24,000
Just act natural.

116
00:06:24,000 --> 00:06:26,000
[fake chuckling]

117
00:06:26,000 --> 00:06:28,000
[Killua] You know what? Forget it.

118
00:06:29,000 --> 00:06:32,000
[Nobunaga] Let’s decide,
right here and now.

119
00:06:33,000 --> 00:06:34,000
Are we going to take him dead,

120
00:06:35,000 --> 00:06:37,000
or try to bring him in alive?

121
00:06:39,000 --> 00:06:40,000
Oh, all right.

122
00:06:45,000 --> 00:06:46,000
Heads.

123
00:06:46,000 --> 00:06:47,000
Tails, then.

124
00:06:50,000 --> 00:06:52,000
HIRUMA MANSION

125
00:06:52,000 --> 00:06:53,000
[Chrollo] Her?

126
00:06:54,000 --> 00:06:55,000
[Shalnark] Yeah.
She’s Nostrade’s daughter.

127
00:06:56,000 --> 00:06:57,000
Her name’s Neon.

128
00:06:58,000 --> 00:07:00,000
According to the information
on the Hunter Website,

129
00:07:00,000 --> 00:07:03,000
the chain user we’re looking
for is one of her bodyguards.

130
00:07:04,000 --> 00:07:06,000
As for the rest of her bodyguards,

131
00:07:06,000 --> 00:07:09,000
we have pictures and names
for these five here.

132
00:07:10,000 --> 00:07:11,000
[Chrollo] This girl…

133
00:07:11,000 --> 00:07:14,000
she’s responsible for Nostrade’s success?

134
00:07:14,000 --> 00:07:15,000
[Shalnark] Most likely.

135
00:07:15,000 --> 00:07:18,000
The info’s on the Hunter website,
so it should be accurate.

136
00:07:23,000 --> 00:07:24,000
[Nostrade] I see.

137
00:07:25,000 --> 00:07:26,000
So that’s what happened.

138
00:07:27,000 --> 00:07:29,000
Getting a new room was a smart move.

139
00:07:29,000 --> 00:07:32,000
The Phantom Troupe
is using the Hunter website;

140
00:07:32,000 --> 00:07:34,000
there’s absolutely no doubt about it.

141
00:07:34,000 --> 00:07:37,000
Neon wouldn’t be safe right now
without your quick thinking.

142
00:07:38,000 --> 00:07:39,000
Thank you.

143
00:07:40,000 --> 00:07:42,000
Now, first things first,

144
00:07:42,000 --> 00:07:44,000
we need to transport
my daughter home urgently.

145
00:07:45,000 --> 00:07:47,000
Is that all right with you, Neon?

146
00:07:48,000 --> 00:07:50,000
It sounds like I don’t have a choice.

147
00:07:50,000 --> 00:07:52,000
With the auction canceled,

148
00:07:52,000 --> 00:07:54,000
I don’t see any point in being here.

149
00:07:54,000 --> 00:07:56,000
And that makes me sad,

150
00:07:56,000 --> 00:07:58,000
because I really wanted to go to that…

151
00:07:59,000 --> 00:08:01,000
They’ll hold another auction
next year, pumpkin.

152
00:08:02,000 --> 00:08:03,000
So, don’t be sad.

153
00:08:03,000 --> 00:08:07,000
And I promise I’ll recover the items
you wanted from those bandits,

154
00:08:07,000 --> 00:08:08,000
if it’s the last thing I do!

155
00:08:08,000 --> 00:08:09,000
[Neon] Really?

156
00:08:10,000 --> 00:08:12,000
Of course, my dear, I promise.

157
00:08:12,000 --> 00:08:15,000
And have I ever in your life
broken a promise to you?

158
00:08:15,000 --> 00:08:18,000
[Neon] Well, yeah…
More than you’ve kept!

159
00:08:18,000 --> 00:08:19,000
[Nostrade laughs]

160
00:08:19,000 --> 00:08:22,000
[Nostrade] All right, you got me.
[chuckles]

161
00:08:22,000 --> 00:08:24,000
Your names are Melody and Basho, yes?

162
00:08:25,000 --> 00:08:26,000
-Yes.
-Yes.

163
00:08:26,000 --> 00:08:29,000
You two take Neon
back to the mansion immediately.

164
00:08:29,000 --> 00:08:30,000
Be safe.

165
00:08:31,000 --> 00:08:33,000
I want you both wearing simple disguises.

166
00:08:35,000 --> 00:08:36,000
Now, Neon.

167
00:08:36,000 --> 00:08:38,000
Go back to your room
and pack up your things.

168
00:08:38,000 --> 00:08:39,000
[Neon] Okay.

169
00:08:42,000 --> 00:08:44,000
[Nostrade] All right.
Let’s get down to business.

170
00:08:47,000 --> 00:08:50,000
The Underground Auction
will be resuming tonight.

171
00:08:50,000 --> 00:08:51,000
[all five] huh?

172
00:08:51,000 --> 00:08:53,000
[Nostrade] The time and place
haven’t changed.

173
00:08:53,000 --> 00:08:55,000
The community must demonstrate

174
00:08:55,000 --> 00:08:57,000
that they will not
be intimidated by anyone.

175
00:08:58,000 --> 00:09:02,000
The Ten Dons have vowed to recover
all of the stolen merchandise.

176
00:09:02,000 --> 00:09:04,000
[Kurapika] But… sir…

177
00:09:04,000 --> 00:09:06,000
As I mentioned earlier,

178
00:09:06,000 --> 00:09:08,000
the man we captured gave up information.

179
00:09:09,000 --> 00:09:10,000
He claimed that a Shadow Beast
took everything

180
00:09:11,000 --> 00:09:13,000
before they even arrived.

181
00:09:14,000 --> 00:09:15,000
Yes, that much is true.

182
00:09:17,000 --> 00:09:20,000
However, all of the Shadow Beasts
are dead.

183
00:09:20,000 --> 00:09:21,000
[both gasp]

184
00:09:21,000 --> 00:09:23,000
[Nostrade] Nine bodies
have been recovered.

185
00:09:24,000 --> 00:09:26,000
The final member, the Owl,

186
00:09:26,000 --> 00:09:30,000
was the one
in charge of transporting the merchandise.

187
00:09:30,000 --> 00:09:32,000
He was probably captured by the Troupe.

188
00:09:33,000 --> 00:09:36,000
The Ten Dons understand
how frightening Nen can be.

189
00:09:36,000 --> 00:09:39,000
If a Troupe member
can compel a confession,

190
00:09:39,000 --> 00:09:41,000
they won’t need to resort to torture.

191
00:09:42,000 --> 00:09:44,000
We think the merchandise the Owl took

192
00:09:44,000 --> 00:09:46,000
has fallen into the Troupe’s hands.

193
00:09:48,000 --> 00:09:50,000
So, as I was just saying,

194
00:09:50,000 --> 00:09:52,000
with all the Shadow Beasts destroyed,

195
00:09:52,000 --> 00:09:55,000
the Ten Dons will hire pros
to handle the Troupe.

196
00:09:56,000 --> 00:09:57,000
Sir?

197
00:09:59,000 --> 00:10:02,000
[Nostrade] The Mafia uses murder
as a tool of intimidation

198
00:10:03,000 --> 00:10:05,000
but it’s not our area of expertise.

199
00:10:06,000 --> 00:10:08,000
Considering the nature of our opponents,

200
00:10:09,000 --> 00:10:12,000
it would be wise for us
to leave it to the experts.

201
00:10:12,000 --> 00:10:15,000
We’ll have them crush the Troupe
on our behalf,

202
00:10:15,000 --> 00:10:18,000
while avoiding further losses ourselves.

203
00:10:19,000 --> 00:10:23,000
However, it’s a chance for us
to build our reputation.

204
00:10:23,000 --> 00:10:26,000
We can’t allow the assassins
to take all the credit.

205
00:10:27,000 --> 00:10:29,000
And so, Kurapika,

206
00:10:29,000 --> 00:10:32,000
I want you to join the assassin team.

207
00:10:41,000 --> 00:10:43,000
[Chrollo] Take care of the chain user
for me.

208
00:10:44,000 --> 00:10:45,000
[Shalnark] Will do.

209
00:10:49,000 --> 00:10:51,000
[Killua] They’re on the move.

210
00:10:51,000 --> 00:10:52,000
Now what?

211
00:10:52,000 --> 00:10:55,000
Like I said,
we can't beat them in a fight.

212
00:10:55,000 --> 00:10:57,000
We’ll figure out a way.

213
00:10:57,000 --> 00:10:59,000
Failure’s not really an option.

214
00:10:59,000 --> 00:11:00,000
He’s right.

215
00:11:00,000 --> 00:11:02,000
We can’t leave empty-handed, not now.

216
00:11:03,000 --> 00:11:04,000
Okay, fine.

217
00:11:05,000 --> 00:11:07,000
But listen. Gon and I will track them.

218
00:11:08,000 --> 00:11:10,000
But no matter what,
we can’t let them spot us.

219
00:11:11,000 --> 00:11:12,000
Which means we’ll have to use Zetsu.

220
00:11:13,000 --> 00:11:14,000
Got it?

221
00:11:17,000 --> 00:11:18,000
Wow...

222
00:11:18,000 --> 00:11:21,000
I can see them standing here
but I can’t sense them.

223
00:11:22,000 --> 00:11:24,000
Hey, Gon. Promise me two things.

224
00:11:25,000 --> 00:11:27,000
If they see us, we give up immediately

225
00:11:27,000 --> 00:11:30,000
and retreat, no questions asked.

226
00:11:30,000 --> 00:11:34,000
Same if I say further pursuit
is impossible for any other reason.

227
00:11:34,000 --> 00:11:35,000
Okay?

228
00:11:35,000 --> 00:11:36,000
[Gon] Okay.

229
00:11:36,000 --> 00:11:39,000
[Killua] The signal to abort
will be one ring.

230
00:11:39,000 --> 00:11:41,000
Make sure your phone is on vibrate.

231
00:11:41,000 --> 00:11:44,000
If they split up, we follow the woman.

232
00:11:44,000 --> 00:11:45,000
Leorio,

233
00:11:45,000 --> 00:11:48,000
call Zepile and keep an eye
on the auction for us.

234
00:11:48,000 --> 00:11:49,000
No problem.

235
00:11:49,000 --> 00:11:52,000
I’m guessing you’ve never
tracked anyone before?

236
00:11:52,000 --> 00:11:54,000
Oh, uh… Yeah, kinda.

237
00:11:54,000 --> 00:11:57,000
I tracked Hisoka during the Exam.

238
00:11:57,000 --> 00:11:58,000
Really? And he didn’t notice you?

239
00:11:59,000 --> 00:12:01,000
No.
I shadowed him pretty much the whole day.

240
00:12:03,000 --> 00:12:05,000
All right! Not too shabby!

241
00:12:06,000 --> 00:12:08,000
That hurt! What did you hit me for?

242
00:12:08,000 --> 00:12:09,000
[Killua] Huh? Oh, no reason.

243
00:12:10,000 --> 00:12:12,000
Well, you shouldn’t have a problem, then.

244
00:12:13,000 --> 00:12:15,000
Just be sure to stay
out of their field of vision,

245
00:12:15,000 --> 00:12:16,000
no matter what.

246
00:12:16,000 --> 00:12:18,000
Ok, ready to go?

247
00:12:18,000 --> 00:12:19,000
[Gon and Leorio] Yeah!

248
00:12:20,000 --> 00:12:24,000
[Killua] The targets have passed the plaza
and gone down a side street.

249
00:12:24,000 --> 00:12:25,000
[Gon] Roger that.

250
00:12:26,000 --> 00:12:27,000
Do you think they know we’re here?

251
00:12:28,000 --> 00:12:29,000
[Killua] It’s fine.

252
00:12:29,000 --> 00:12:32,000
We’re using Zetsu,
so they won’t unless something goes wrong.

253
00:12:32,000 --> 00:12:34,000
But they’re expecting someone
to follow them,

254
00:12:34,000 --> 00:12:36,000
so be careful.

255
00:12:36,000 --> 00:12:38,000
Okay. You too, Killua.

256
00:12:38,000 --> 00:12:42,000
Ugh... He’s really telling me
to be careful?

257
00:12:42,000 --> 00:12:43,000
I’m the one on high alert,

258
00:12:44,000 --> 00:12:45,000
looking for changes in their behavior!

259
00:12:50,000 --> 00:12:51,000
Good.

260
00:12:51,000 --> 00:12:52,000
They haven’t noticed us.

261
00:12:53,000 --> 00:12:55,000
When they realize we’re here,

262
00:12:55,000 --> 00:12:56,000
they’re bound to react somehow.

263
00:12:57,000 --> 00:12:59,000
They can try to hide it,

264
00:12:59,000 --> 00:13:02,000
but their faces or gestures
will give them away.

265
00:13:04,000 --> 00:13:06,000
I’ve been playing life-or-death games
of ‘shadow’

266
00:13:06,000 --> 00:13:08,000
ever since I was three.

267
00:13:09,000 --> 00:13:11,000
I won’t lose sight of them.

268
00:13:11,000 --> 00:13:12,000
I can’t!

269
00:13:14,000 --> 00:13:16,000
Are we being followed?

270
00:13:16,000 --> 00:13:18,000
Yes, most likely.

271
00:13:18,000 --> 00:13:19,000
It’s a pretty good bet, anyway.

272
00:13:20,000 --> 00:13:22,000
Guess they know what they’re doing.

273
00:13:22,000 --> 00:13:24,000
I don’t sense a damn thing.

274
00:13:25,000 --> 00:13:27,000
They must be quite skilled.

275
00:13:42,000 --> 00:13:45,000
[Killua] Damn, they’re moving
toward a deserted part of the city.

276
00:13:47,000 --> 00:13:49,000
Maybe they figured out
they’re being followed.

277
00:13:50,000 --> 00:13:52,000
So, could this be a trap?

278
00:13:52,000 --> 00:13:53,000
No…

279
00:13:54,000 --> 00:13:56,000
They don’t know our exact locations.

280
00:13:56,000 --> 00:13:58,000
Unless they don’t know
they’re being followed

281
00:13:58,000 --> 00:14:00,000
and they’re heading back to their hideout.

282
00:14:01,000 --> 00:14:03,000
That’d be a huge win for us.

283
00:14:04,000 --> 00:14:05,000
So, a trap...

284
00:14:06,000 --> 00:14:07,000
or their hideout?

285
00:14:07,000 --> 00:14:08,000
Which is it?

286
00:14:09,000 --> 00:14:11,000
If it’s a trap, we bail.

287
00:14:11,000 --> 00:14:13,000
Hideout, we keep following them.

288
00:14:17,000 --> 00:14:20,000
There’s nothing unnatural
in their behavior.

289
00:14:20,000 --> 00:14:21,000
We keep going!

290
00:14:28,000 --> 00:14:30,000
Our stalker isn’t taking the bait.

291
00:14:30,000 --> 00:14:33,000
Which means that it’s probably
not the chain user.

292
00:14:33,000 --> 00:14:34,000
[Machi] Why’s that?

293
00:14:34,000 --> 00:14:37,000
[Nobunaga] I can sense
multiple people tailing us

294
00:14:38,000 --> 00:14:39,000
but the chain user…

295
00:14:39,000 --> 00:14:41,000
probably works alone.

296
00:14:41,000 --> 00:14:42,000
[Machi] Think so?

297
00:14:42,000 --> 00:14:46,000
Yeah, he works as a bodyguard
for the Nostrade family, right?

298
00:14:46,000 --> 00:14:49,000
Yet he managed to defeat Uvo
completely on his own,

299
00:14:49,000 --> 00:14:50,000
and that’s no easy task.

300
00:14:51,000 --> 00:14:53,000
But the Mafia hasn’t taken any action,

301
00:14:53,000 --> 00:14:55,000
which supports my theory.

302
00:14:55,000 --> 00:14:57,000
If they were responsible,

303
00:14:57,000 --> 00:14:59,000
they’d be using Uvo to threaten us

304
00:15:00,000 --> 00:15:01,000
whether he was dead or alive.

305
00:15:02,000 --> 00:15:06,000
Not to mention the news
would probably be all over the web by now.

306
00:15:07,000 --> 00:15:11,000
Since it’s not the chain user
probably defeated Uvo alone,

307
00:15:11,000 --> 00:15:13,000
without ever reporting it to the Mafia.

308
00:15:14,000 --> 00:15:15,000
Doesn’t make sense.

309
00:15:16,000 --> 00:15:19,000
Why would someone with ties to the Mafia
work alone?

310
00:15:21,000 --> 00:15:23,000
Probably a personal grudge.

311
00:15:23,000 --> 00:15:26,000
“Probably”, huh?
You’ve been saying that a lot.

312
00:15:26,000 --> 00:15:27,000
Oh, shut up.

313
00:15:27,000 --> 00:15:31,000
If he went out seeking revenge
without Mafia backup,

314
00:15:31,000 --> 00:15:33,000
I doubt that he’d be
teaming up with someone else.

315
00:15:34,000 --> 00:15:36,000
Thus, the chain user works alone.

316
00:15:36,000 --> 00:15:39,000
The group following us
is totally unrelated.

317
00:15:39,000 --> 00:15:42,000
Impressive how full of holes
your logic is.

318
00:15:42,000 --> 00:15:45,000
Okay, fine then Let’s hear what you think.

319
00:15:45,000 --> 00:15:46,000
All right.

320
00:15:46,000 --> 00:15:48,000
If you really must know…

321
00:15:48,000 --> 00:15:52,000
I suspect that there’s a link
between these guys and the chain user.

322
00:15:54,000 --> 00:15:55,000
Hunch again?

323
00:15:55,000 --> 00:15:56,000
It is.

324
00:15:56,000 --> 00:15:58,000
You’ve gotta be kidding.

325
00:15:58,000 --> 00:16:00,000
People who rely on their gut feelings

326
00:16:00,000 --> 00:16:02,000
really shouldn’t criticize
someone else’s logic.

327
00:16:03,000 --> 00:16:04,000
So, what do you think?

328
00:16:04,000 --> 00:16:07,000
[Killua] They’re waiting for someone,
or trying to draw us out.

329
00:16:07,000 --> 00:16:08,000
One or the other.

330
00:16:09,000 --> 00:16:11,000
Yeah, but do you think
they know we’re following them?

331
00:16:11,000 --> 00:16:13,000
[Killua] Right now, it’s fifty-fifty.

332
00:16:13,000 --> 00:16:15,000
But they definitely don’t know
our location.

333
00:16:16,000 --> 00:16:17,000
That’s why they’re trying to lure us out.

334
00:16:18,000 --> 00:16:20,000
They want us to show ourselves.

335
00:16:20,000 --> 00:16:21,000
[Gon] What do we do?

336
00:16:22,000 --> 00:16:24,000
[Killua] They might be waiting
for someone else.

337
00:16:24,000 --> 00:16:26,000
-Hold your position.
-[phone ringing]

338
00:16:27,000 --> 00:16:28,000
Gon, I’m hanging up.

339
00:16:29,000 --> 00:16:30,000
-[phone ringing]
-Pay close attention

340
00:16:31,000 --> 00:16:32,000
and if they react at all,

341
00:16:32,000 --> 00:16:34,000
we’re gonna make a run for it.
And don’t stop!

342
00:16:35,000 --> 00:16:37,000
The next time I ring it means we bail.

343
00:16:39,000 --> 00:16:40,000
Yeah, I got it.

344
00:16:41,000 --> 00:16:42,000
[Phinks] It’s Phinks.

345
00:16:42,000 --> 00:16:43,000
Oh, what’s up, Phinks?

346
00:16:44,000 --> 00:16:46,000
[Phinks] Just wanted to see
how you’re doing.

347
00:16:46,000 --> 00:16:48,000
We were being followed for a while

348
00:16:49,000 --> 00:16:50,000
but they haven’t made their move.

349
00:16:50,000 --> 00:16:52,000
And we can’t locate them,

350
00:16:52,000 --> 00:16:53,000
so this’ll take some time.

351
00:16:54,000 --> 00:16:55,000
[Phinks] Oh, yeah?

352
00:16:55,000 --> 00:16:57,000
Then how about a hint?

353
00:16:57,000 --> 00:16:59,000
Wait, what are you talking about?

354
00:17:08,000 --> 00:17:09,000
[gasping in shock]

355
00:17:36,000 --> 00:17:37,000
[grunts]

356
00:17:40,000 --> 00:17:41,000
A diversion?

357
00:17:41,000 --> 00:17:43,000
Got him!!

358
00:17:44,000 --> 00:17:45,000
He blocked it easily,

359
00:17:45,000 --> 00:17:46,000
with his left hand!

360
00:17:49,000 --> 00:17:51,000
[straining]

361
00:17:52,000 --> 00:17:53,000
[Killua roars]

362
00:17:53,000 --> 00:17:54,000
[whistles]

363
00:17:58,000 --> 00:17:59,000
[Nobunaga] Hey.

364
00:17:59,000 --> 00:18:00,000
[Killua gasps]

365
00:18:00,000 --> 00:18:01,000
Hello, Phinks.

366
00:18:02,000 --> 00:18:03,000
What are you doing here?

367
00:18:04,000 --> 00:18:07,000
I swear I was told
that you were heading out with the Boss.

368
00:18:07,000 --> 00:18:09,000
This is the fourth floor!

369
00:18:09,000 --> 00:18:10,000
Well, like they say,

370
00:18:10,000 --> 00:18:12,000
“deceive your allies
to deceive your enemies”.

371
00:18:13,000 --> 00:18:14,000
[shrill chuckle]

372
00:18:14,000 --> 00:18:16,000
Looks like the Boss got me good again.

373
00:18:17,000 --> 00:18:19,000
Zetsu masters all over the place?

374
00:18:19,000 --> 00:18:20,000
Guess I should’ve known…

375
00:18:21,000 --> 00:18:24,000
They tailed us while we tailed them?
And our targets didn’t know?!

376
00:18:25,000 --> 00:18:26,000
They tricked us!

377
00:18:26,000 --> 00:18:28,000
[Nobunaga] So, kiddo…

378
00:18:28,000 --> 00:18:30,000
I’ve got a couple of questions for you.

379
00:18:35,000 --> 00:18:38,000
Do you know the chain user
and think before you answer.

380
00:18:40,000 --> 00:18:43,000
He’s a Nen user who fights with chains.

381
00:18:43,000 --> 00:18:45,000
We’re trying to find him.

382
00:18:45,000 --> 00:18:47,000
Is he the one who asked you to follow us?

383
00:18:48,000 --> 00:18:49,000
Was this his idea?

384
00:18:49,000 --> 00:18:51,000
[Gon] I don’t know him.

385
00:18:51,000 --> 00:18:54,000
We followed you two for our own reasons
and not anybody else’s.

386
00:18:55,000 --> 00:18:57,000
I just need a split second,

387
00:18:57,000 --> 00:18:59,000
an opening, to get away!

388
00:19:00,000 --> 00:19:01,000
Your thoughts?

389
00:19:02,000 --> 00:19:03,000
I just can’t tell...

390
00:19:04,000 --> 00:19:06,000
If he’s lying, he’s certainly good at it.

391
00:19:07,000 --> 00:19:08,000
Why don’t I check.

392
00:19:09,000 --> 00:19:11,000
[Nobunaga] Question one:

393
00:19:11,000 --> 00:19:13,000
Why were you following us?

394
00:19:13,000 --> 00:19:14,000
Be concise.

395
00:19:16,000 --> 00:19:18,000
A bad lie will make things worse.

396
00:19:19,000 --> 00:19:23,000
Because the Mafia has put out
a huge bounty on your heads.

397
00:19:24,000 --> 00:19:25,000
Websites are offering a lot of money

398
00:19:25,000 --> 00:19:28,000
just for information on your whereabouts.

399
00:19:28,000 --> 00:19:30,000
[Nobunaga] Question two:

400
00:19:30,000 --> 00:19:32,000
Who taught you to track people?

401
00:19:32,000 --> 00:19:33,000
I guess mainly...

402
00:19:34,000 --> 00:19:38,000
I used a Nen ability
to hide myself called Zetsu.

403
00:19:38,000 --> 00:19:40,000
See, I... want to be a pro Hunter.

404
00:19:41,000 --> 00:19:43,000
Who taught you to do that?

405
00:19:43,000 --> 00:19:45,000
It was a Shingen-ryu master.

406
00:19:45,000 --> 00:19:47,000
And three:

407
00:19:47,000 --> 00:19:50,000
Do you know a Nen user
who fights with chains?

408
00:19:50,000 --> 00:19:52,000
Fights with chains?

409
00:19:52,000 --> 00:19:54,000
[Nobunaga]
He’d be a Conjurer or Manipulator.

410
00:19:55,000 --> 00:19:59,000
We want to know if your master
has chains hanging from his right arm.

411
00:19:59,000 --> 00:20:00,000
Or is it you?

412
00:20:01,000 --> 00:20:03,000
You should come clean right now if it is.

413
00:20:03,000 --> 00:20:05,000
I really don’t know.

414
00:20:05,000 --> 00:20:07,000
My master is an Enhancer and...

415
00:20:07,000 --> 00:20:11,000
he just taught me
the four basic exercises, nothing more.

416
00:20:11,000 --> 00:20:13,000
Well, that’s a pity.

417
00:20:13,000 --> 00:20:15,000
If you don’t know, we got nothin.

418
00:20:15,000 --> 00:20:17,000
It’s time for the last question.

419
00:20:17,000 --> 00:20:19,000
I’ll give you two choices

420
00:20:19,000 --> 00:20:21,000
but think carefully before you answer.

421
00:20:22,000 --> 00:20:25,000
Do you want to die now or later?

422
00:20:25,000 --> 00:20:26,000
It’s up to you.

423
00:20:27,000 --> 00:20:29,000
You have three seconds.

424
00:20:31,000 --> 00:20:32,000
[terrified breath]

425
00:20:32,000 --> 00:20:34,000
[phone buzzing]

426
00:20:37,000 --> 00:20:39,000
It’s no use. Don’t try anything.

427
00:20:39,000 --> 00:20:40,000
Yes.

428
00:20:41,000 --> 00:20:42,000
Understood. On our way.

429
00:20:43,000 --> 00:20:44,000
Little boy.

430
00:20:44,000 --> 00:20:47,000
That friend of yours
surrendered quietly.

431
00:20:50,000 --> 00:20:51,000
[Pakunoda] I’ll ask again.

432
00:20:51,000 --> 00:20:53,000
Do you know the chain user?

433
00:20:53,000 --> 00:20:55,000
I already told you that before.

434
00:20:55,000 --> 00:20:56,000
I don’t!

435
00:20:56,000 --> 00:20:57,000
I see.

436
00:20:58,000 --> 00:20:59,000
What about you, boy?

437
00:21:00,000 --> 00:21:01,000
Do you have any guesses?

438
00:21:02,000 --> 00:21:03,000
[tires screeching]

439
00:21:24,000 --> 00:21:26,000
Welcome to our hideout.

440
00:21:26,000 --> 00:21:27,000
[both gasp]

441
00:21:32,000 --> 00:21:34,000
[narrator] Gon and Killua find themselves

442
00:21:34,000 --> 00:21:38,000
standing inside the hideout
of the dreaded Phantom Troupe,

443
00:21:39,000 --> 00:21:42,000
gripped by the anticipation
of what’s to come.

444
00:21:44,000 --> 00:21:47,000
[theme song playing]

445
00:22:53,000 --> 00:22:54,000
[Gon] Coming up:

446
00:22:54,000 --> 00:22:55,000
-Gon...
-[Killua] ...and Killua’s…

447
00:22:55,000 --> 00:22:57,000
[both] Hunterpedia!

448
00:22:57,000 --> 00:22:59,000
-I’m Gon!
-I’m Killua!

449
00:22:59,000 --> 00:23:00,000
[both] And this is our Hunterpedia!

450
00:23:00,000 --> 00:23:02,000
Today, we're introducing Machi!

451
00:23:02,000 --> 00:23:04,000
She’s Phantom Troupe
and she’s a Transmuter!

452
00:23:04,000 --> 00:23:06,000
She can turn her aura into Nen threads.

453
00:23:06,000 --> 00:23:08,000
Her big technique is Nen stitches.

454
00:23:08,000 --> 00:23:09,000
She can put your body back together!

455
00:23:09,000 --> 00:23:11,000
[both] Just like this!

456
00:23:15,000 --> 00:23:16,000
[Gon] Next time: “Ally x and x Sword”.

457
00:23:17,000 --> 00:23:18,000
-Gotcha!
-[Killua buzzing like mosquito]

458
00:23:19,000 --> 00:23:21,000
[Gon] Hey! Look! I caught it!

459
00:23:21,000 --> 00:23:22,000
[Killua] That’s one of Milluki’s
mini-bombs!

460
00:23:23,000 --> 00:23:24,000
[Gon and Killua] Ka-boom!
